<p><strong>Direct Answer:</strong> Managing time-sensitive short links requires configuring automatic expiration dates, utilizing dynamic redirects, and communicating clear urgency within the custom slug. For campaigns like flash sales, webinar registrations, or limited-time offers, leaving a link active after the event concludes creates a poor user experience and damages brand credibility. By setting a definitive expiration protocol, you ensure that late clickers are seamlessly redirected to a relevant fallback page, such as a "Sale Ended" notice or a newsletter signup form. This practice matters because it preserves link equity, prevents frustrating 404 errors, and allows you to capture residual traffic that would otherwise be lost. Implementing strict best practices for temporary links maximizes your short-term conversion windows while maintaining long-term digital hygiene.</p>

